OK, as some other posts pointed out you may ask a shopkeeper.
Failing that (yes, I had a game not long ago, where the main dungeon had only
armor and potions shops up to level 8, and mines were without a general 
store either) you just collect many scrolls (20-30) and read the ones you 
have most copies of. Id is the most common scroll, other common ones are 
also safe (if not cursed) - so statistics is on your side.

Finally I must say I tried recently to apply this strategy very consequently, 
and I  noticed, that the average life span of my characters seems to have 
improved since. So maybe it is not completely stupid - through as the result
some of my characters read their firs scroll 10000 moves into the game...
